  "how_to_read_this": "A rank correlation near one means the metric orders architectures the way perplexity already does, so reporting it adds a column and not a fact. A moderate correlation is the case for the battery: the metric and the objective disagree about which architectures are better, and the disagreement is what a single-metric evaluation cannot see.",
  "why_sign_is_not_interpreted_as_quality": "Each metric has its own direction \u2014 higher BLiMP is better, lower calibration error is better \u2014 so the sign of a correlation with perplexity follows from that direction and carries no separate meaning. Only the magnitude is read."
